<text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
  <body>
    <div rend="parallel"> 
      <p xml:id="Aink161-kilavi">
        oruvaḻi taṇantuḻi āṟṟuvikkuntōḻikkut talaimakaḷ āṟṟāḷāyc colliyatu.</p>    <p xml:lang="en">
        Spoken by the heroine as one who could not bear it, to the confidante who comforts [her], when [the hero] departed [his] own way. </p>
  </div>  
    <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="Aink161">
<l>peruṅkaṭaṟ karaiyatu ciṟuveṇ kākkai</l>
<l>karuṅkōṭṭup puṉṉait taṅkun tuṟaivaṟkup</l>
<l>pacantunuta laḻiyac cāay</l>
<l>nayanta neñca nōyppā laḵtē</l>
      </lg>
      <lg xml:lang="en">
        <l>As for the words of the man from the seashore</l>
        <l>In which the small, white crow of the vast seashore</l>
        <l>Rests in a grove in which flowers are fragrant,</l>
        <l>After having seatched for meat in the backwaters of a dark nature, having swum [there],</l>
        <l>They have become something else! [= lies]</l>      </lg>
    </div>
  </body>
</text>
